---
# ansible/.ansible-lint
#
# BUG-4 (ansible-lint policy): fix the real violations in code (see
# site.yml/group_vars/all.yml -- no-changed-when, yaml[truthy], and the
# `ignore-errors` restructure), and config-ignore only the ONE rule that
# fires against a deliberate, reviewed convention rather than a real
# defect:
#
#   name[casing] -- "names should start uppercase". Every task name in
#   this playbook is deliberately prefixed with its act/stage marker in
#   lowercase (`act1: ...`, `act3: ...`, `act4: ...`, `act5: ...`,
#   `act6: ...`, `pre: ...`, `AC-4: ...`) because ansible/tests/*.sh's
#   AC-order/AC-env grep-based structural checks match on those EXACT,
#   lowercase-first task-name markers (see layer1-static.sh's
#   `grep -n 'act4: harden the 8 LOCKED enforcement paths'` /
#   `grep -n 'act5: lock the G-3 key'` / the AC-4 awk block). Renaming
#   every task to start uppercase would either break that grep contract or
#   require restating the act/stage marker twice (once for lint, once for
#   the grep anchor) -- config-ignoring this one cosmetic rule is more
#   honest than papering over it with a redundant naming scheme. This does
#   NOT rename any task.
#
# `ignore-errors` is intentionally NOT in this list: the former
# `ignore_errors: "{{ item.tolerate_absent | default(false) }}"` use on
# act 4 (which this rule flagged) was replaced with an explicit
# stat-then-fail/skip structure in site.yml, so there is no remaining
# `ignore_errors:` use to suppress (BUG-4's "pick the honest one" ->
# the code fix, not a config suppression).
skip_list:
  - name[casing]
